{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011Cf6i6HSGY8JsmUaDzZYSY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now I have a complete understanding. Let me summarize the analysis:\n\n**Repository findings:**\n- Order entity at `Order.kt:11` - currently has no status field\n- OrderController at `OrderController.kt:16` - injects repository, throws exceptions for errors\n- OrderRepository at `OrderRepository.kt:10` - simple in-memory ConcurrentHashMap\n- Shipment entity at `Shipment.kt:9` - already has ShipmentStatus enum (CREATED, CONFIRMED, CANCELLED)\n- ShipmentController at `ShipmentController.kt:22` - follows same pattern as OrderController\n- ShipmentRepository at `ShipmentRepository.kt:11` - needs method to find shipments by orderId\n- Error handling via ApiException subclasses at `ApiExceptions.kt:11` - ResourceNotFoundException and ConflictException\n- ErrorCode enum at `ApiError.kt:31` - needs new codes\n- GlobalExceptionHandler at `GlobalExceptionHandler.kt:13` - centralized error mapping\n\n**Conventions this repository has:**\n- All errors thrown as ApiException subclasses from controllers/services\n- HTTP status codes determined by exception type (ResourceNotFoundException→404, ConflictException→409)\n- Centralized error envelope with code, message, fields\n- In-memory repositories with simple CRUD methods\n- Tests clear repository in @BeforeEach and use MockMvc with jsonPath assertions\n- Status tracking via enums (ShipmentStatus example)\n- Status field is part of the entity data class\n\n**Affected files:** Order.kt, OrderController.kt, OrderRepository.kt, ShipmentRepository.kt, ApiError.kt, ShipmentController.kt, OrderControllerTest.kt, ShipmentControllerTest.kt\n\n**Risks:** Breaking changes to Order serialization if status field added; atomicity of cancel (must check all shipments before cancelling any); all-or-nothing semantics.\n\n**Open questions:** None - requirement is clear.\n\n---\n\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n\n**Proposed change:**\n\n1. **Order.kt** - Add OrderStatus enum with ACTIVE, CANCELLED values. Add optional status field to Order data class (default ACTIVE for new orders, persisted by repository).\n\n2. **OrderController.kt** - Add `@PostMapping(\"/{orderId}/cancel\")` endpoint that:\n   - Looks up the order, throws ResourceNotFoundException if not found (404)\n   - Gets all shipments for that order from ShipmentRepository\n   - Checks if ANY shipment has CONFIRMED status; if so, throw ConflictException (409) with SHIPMENT_CONFIRMED_CONFLICT code\n   - If checks pass, update order to CANCELLED status\n   - Update all CREATED shipments to CANCELLED status  \n   - Return updated order with 200 status\n   - Idempotent: if order already CANCELLED, succeed and return it\n\n3. **OrderRepository.kt** - Add `findByOrderId(orderId: String): List<Shipment>` method to ShipmentRepository. Actually, this goes in ShipmentRepository.\n\n4. **ShipmentRepository.kt** - Add `findByOrderId(orderId: String): List<Shipment>` to find all shipments for an order.\n\n5. **ApiError.kt** - Add two new error codes: `ORDER_CANCELLED` (for when trying to create shipment for cancelled order), `SHIPMENT_CONFIRMED_CONFLICT` (for when trying to cancel order with confirmed shipment).\n\n6. **ShipmentController.kt** - Modify create endpoint to:\n   - Check if order exists first (ResourceNotFoundException if not - per requirement \"keeps its current behaviour\")\n   - Check if order status is CANCELLED; if so, throw ConflictException with ORDER_CANCELLED code (409)\n   - Otherwise proceed with creation\n\n7. **OrderControllerTest.kt** - Add tests for:\n   - Cancel active order (success, 200)\n   - Cancel already-cancelled order (success, idempotent)\n   - Cancel with confirmed shipment (409, no changes)\n   - Cancel non-existent order (404)\n   - Verify order status in response\n   - Verify created shipment is cancelled\n\n8. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** - Add test for:\n   - Creating shipment for cancelled order (409 with ORDER_CANCELLED code)\n\n**Alternative rejected:**\nCould store cancel timestamp instead of status enum, but the requirement explicitly states \"a status\" with ACTIVE and CANCELLED values, so enum is the right approach.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\nFor cancel success flow:\n1. Request: `POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel` (no body)\n2. Controller looks up order by ID\n3. If not found → ResourceNotFoundException (404 ORDER_NOT_FOUND)\n4. Get all shipments for this order\n5. Check if any has CONFIRMED status → ConflictException (409 SHIPMENT_CONFIRMED_CONFLICT), nothing changes\n6. Update order status to CANCELLED\n7. For each shipment with CREATED status, update to CANCELLED\n8. Return 200 with updated Order (includes new status field)\n\nFor create shipment flow:\n1. Request: `POST /shipments` with orderId\n2. Controller checks if order exists (using repository)\n3. If not found → ResourceNotFoundException (404 ORDER_NOT_FOUND) - unchanged behavior\n4. If order status is CANCELLED → ConflictException (409 ORDER_CANCELLED)\n5. Otherwise proceed with creation\n\nFor idempotent cancel:\n1. If order already CANCELLED when cancel is called, just return 200 with order\n2. No changes to shipments, no errors\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\nOrderControllerTest additions:\n- `test_cancel_active_order_succeeds()` - Creates ACTIVE order, calls cancel, expects 200 with CANCELLED status\n- `test_cancel_already_cancelled_order_succeeds()` - Creates order, cancels, cancels again, expects 200 (idempotent)\n- `test_cancel_order_with_confirmed_shipment_fails()` - Creates order, creates CONFIRMED shipment (using repository.save directly), tries cancel, expects 409, verifies order still ACTIVE\n- `test_cancel_nonexistent_order_fails()` - Tries cancel on missing order, expects 404\n- `test_cancel_order_cancels_created_shipments()` - Creates order with multiple CREATED shipments, cancels, verifies shipments now CANCELLED\n\nShipmentControllerTest addit